    "result_text": "Tests are green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with both findings and restructured the rejection side to match the project's idiom (one dedicated checked exception + escalation handler per failure mode):\n\n- **New `DisposableEmailException`** (checked) with its own message, `\"Email domain is not accepted: \" + email` \u2014 distinct from the syntax error.\n- **New `DisposableEmailExceptionHandler`** responding 400 with the same `OwnerFieldErrors([\"email\"])` contract as the other owner-field validators.\n- **New escalation YAML** `\u2026owner.DisposableEmailException.yml` wiring the handler.\n- **`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** now throws `DisposableEmailException` from the blocklist branch (and declares both exceptions in its `throws`), so the two distinct `if` blocks no longer throw the identical exception. Updated its javadoc.\n- **`InvalidEmailException`** is left untouched, so its javadoc and `\"...syntactically valid address...\"` message are once again accurate \u2014 it means only \"syntactically invalid.\"\n\nThe `OwnerEmail` centralisation (`isDisposable` + `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS`) the review praised is unchanged. Acceptance behaviour is intact \u2014 `x@mailinator.com` still returns 400 \u2014 and the suite passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
